# {{name}}

A Go service scaffolded by `pnpm gen service`. It follows `.claude/rules/go-service-architecture.md`:

```
main.go                       composition root: the only file that wires concrete adapters
internal/config/              environment -> Config, validated at startup (the only os.Getenv)
internal/adapter/httpapi/     transport: probes, request logging, panic recovery, your routes
```

Add `internal/core/` (stdlib only, declares the ports it needs) when there is a business
decision to make, and outbound adapters under `internal/adapter/<x>/` when it talks to a database,
a queue or another service. Wire them in `main.go`.

## Run

```sh
cd apps/{{name}} && go run .        # or `air` for hot reload
curl localhost:{{port}}/healthz
```

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `LISTEN_ADDR` | `:{{port}}` | Address the server listens on. |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `10s` | Grace period for in-flight requests on shutdown. |

## Build and deploy

```sh
docker build -f apps/{{name}}/Dockerfile -t {{name}} .   # context is the repo root
```

Kubernetes manifests live under `infrastructure/kubernetes/<environment>/<namespace>/{{name}}/`.
Replace the `ghcr.io/OWNER/ignition-{{name}}` image placeholder before deploying.
